{# <twig:c975LBook:Contributor:Hero contributor="{{ contributor }}" [editUrl=""] />. Same opening as a serie's, the portrait standing where a serie shows its cover, and the only hero carrying its own summary: a person is introduced right beside their portrait, where a book keeps its blurb for a block under the hero. Carries the page's only h1 - contributor/display.html.twig leaves the layout's title block empty. The page opens on a background image when one is uploaded: a real <img> and a veil above it, never a background-image - a nonce style-src covers no style attribute (see Book:Hero) #}
{% props contributor, editUrl = "" %}
{% set background = contributor.backgrounds|first != false ? contributor.backgrounds|first : '' %}
<header class="book-hero book-page__hero{{ background ? ' book-hero--has-bg' : '' }}"{% if editUrl %} data-block-edit-url="{{ editUrl }}"{% endif %}>
    {% if background %}
        <img class="book-hero__bg" src="{{ asset(background) }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true" fetchpriority="high">
        <div class="book-hero__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    {% endif %}

    {% set portraitSrc = contributor.portraits|first != false ? contributor.portraits|first : "bundles/c975lbook/images/no-cover.webp" %}
    <img class="book-hero__cover" src="{{ asset(portraitSrc) }}" alt="{{ contributor.name }}" width="240" fetchpriority="high">

    <div class="book-hero__body">
        <h1 class="book-hero__title">{{ contributor.name }}</h1>

        {# What they are credited under, read from what credits them rather than from a field of their own (see Contributor::getRoles()): the two columns of a book first, then the parts its rows name #}
        {% if contributor.roles|length %}
            <p class="book-hero__roles">{{ contributor.roles|map(role => book_role_label(role))|join(' · ') }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        {# The sentences they are introduced with, unfolded whole: the number of books they signed used to stand here, and it said "6 livres" over the very list printing them - a site naming its catalog "Toutes nos histoires" read "6 toutes nos histoires". A div rather than a p, the field being written in a rich text editor whose own blocks stand #}
        {% if contributor.summary %}
            <div class="book-hero__summary">{{ contributor.summary|raw }}</div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if contributor.website %}
            <p class="book-hero__meta">
                <a href="{{ contributor.website }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ 'label.website'|trans({}, 'book') }}</a>
            </p>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</header>
